  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Chronic cough with wheeze and breathlessness since his late thirties, worse every winter and within a day of any stay in the city or by an open fire, better in warm weather and country air; night cough two or three times a week this winter; under evaluation</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R05.3</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem echoing his documented lifelong cough and breathlessness in London&apos;s coal smoke; superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Long exposure to urban air pollution (decades in a large city with heavy traffic and coal and wood burning) and to indoor solid-fuel smoke from open coal and wood fires at home</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z77.110</td><td>S — Synthetic modern exposure echoing the coal smoke that he, Sydenham, and Lady Masham blamed for his cough; no historical level of exposure is asserted.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

