<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Diagnostic workup: spirometry before and after bronchodilator, FeNO, DLCO, blood count with eosinophils, total IgE, alpha-1 antitrypsin, NT-proBNP, interferon-gamma release assay, chest X-ray, and CT of the chest if airflow limitation persists after bronchodilator; albuterol withheld for 6 hours before testing. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma and COPD monographs (2026); Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); Global Strategy for the Prevention, Diagnosis and Management of COPD: 2025 Report (2025); Stanojevic S, et al. ERS/ATS technical standard on interpretive strategies for routine lung function tests. Eur Respir J 2022;60(1):2101499 (PMID 34949706) (2022); Bhakta NR, et al. Race and Ethnicity in Pulmonary Function Test Interpretation: An Official American Thoracic Society Statement. Am J Respir Crit Care Med 2023;207(8):978-995 (PMID 36973004) (2023) [S]</item><item>Exposure reduction from today: no open coal or wood fires in his rooms (electric or heat-pump heating instead); a portable HEPA air cleaner sized for his study and bedroom; daily check of the air quality index, with city trips and outdoor exertion avoided on alert days; a well-fitted N95 respirator on unavoidable high-pollution days; quieter routes away from main roads. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma and COPD monographs (2026); Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); WHO global air quality guidelines: particulate matter (PM2.5 and PM10), ozone, nitrogen dioxide, sulfur dioxide and carbon monoxide (2021); Carlsten C, et al. Personal strategies to minimise effects of air pollution on respiratory health: advice for providers, patients and the public. Eur Respir J 2020;55(6):1902056 (PMID 32241830) (2020); AQI Basics (2026); Air Cleaners and Air Filters in the Home (2026) [S]</item><item>Pulmonology consultation on the diagnosis (asthma, COPD, or both), the need for CT, treatment, and pulmonary rehabilitation. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma and COPD monographs (2026); Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); Global Strategy for the Prevention, Diagnosis and Management of COPD: 2025 Report (2025) [S]</item><item>Vaccinations: pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 at the diagnosis visit; influenza, COVID-19, and RSV vaccines in the autumn; recombinant zoster vaccine. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma and COPD monographs (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026) [S]</item><item>Monitoring: Asthma Control Test, inhaler technique, adherence, reliever use, and exposures at every visit; spirometry and FeNO 3 months after starting treatment, then every 1 to 2 years; home peak flow diary. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma and COPD monographs (2026); Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
